      "analysis": "The relevant task is Problem A, tropical.cpp, on four ARM64 CPU cores. Baseline averages 5.265 ms; const-reference A averages 5.154 ms, incremental-search B 5.191 ms and sibling-parallel C 5.221 ms. These small differences are below the baseline's observed 0.457 ms sample range, so they are tentative gains, not established speedups. Contiguous matrices (6.616 ms), cached neighbors (6.765 ms) and parallel roots (7.901 ms) measured worse. Prioritize low-overhead serial transformations and measured integration. Source costs include pervasive copies, map-backed traversal and repeated partition/path allocations. Preserve deterministic reference traversal and output; passing four correctness cases does not establish correctness for every valid input."
